SAY ~How dare he! Powerful or not, slaves deserve instant death for even daring to touch one of their betters. But torture.... fear not, I will remove his head personally.~ 
++ ~Slave? I seriously doubt that he is anyone's slave. Besides, slavery is illegal in Athkatla.~  + FT1b
++ ~Irenicus is too powerful and too dangerous for that, slaves that cannot be controlled are useless. That and he has committed too many horrors to be allowed to live.~  + FT1g
++ ~Slavery is illegal in Athkatla, Navarra. Please do not make me regret bringing you along.~ + FT1i
++ ~I do not care to continue this discussion. Let's go.~  EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1b
SAY ~Illegal? That makes no sense... what else are males good for other than begetting offspring?~ 
++ ~You must be joking...right? I do not know what it is like where you come from but here, men are treated as equals and contribute much in many ways.~  + FT1w
++ ~I wonder that myself sometimes. Having slaves to pamper you and serve of you.. now that would be nice.~ + FT1za
++ ~It seems you have a lot to learn about the way the things work around here.~ + FT1c
++ ~Yes, illegal. And that includes you so do not get any ideas. I will not tolerate it.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1g
SAY ~And he will die, I promise you that. We seem to be like minded about slaves, <CHARNAME>, have you owned slaves as well?~
++ ~While I agree with you as far as slaves that cannot be controlled are useless, I would never own another person. It is wrong to rob someone of thier freedom.~ + FT1h
++ ~Sadly, I have not and most likely never will. The best I can hope for is finding a man who will do it willingly.~ + FT1o
++ ~Certainly not. I do hope, however, that I get to torture Irenicus before he dies.~ + FT1p
++ ~Maybe, maybe not. But it does not matter, we need to get going and find Imoen.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1w
SAY ~It would seem so..... I assumed from what I saw in the Promenade that slaves were common here.~ 
++ ~What would make you think that? I did not notice anyone being treated that way.~ + FT1x
++ ~I did notice a few questionable characters but I am not sure what would lead you to that conclusion. Or maybe it is because I already knew it was illegal here.~ + FT1y
++ ~I suppose I can see why you would draw that conclusion but you should be careful calling people that in the future.~ + FT1z
++ ~If you say so. I think it is time we get going.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1i
SAY ~Do not make me regret trusting you.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1t
SAY ~Fair enough, I am here if you wish to talk about it.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1c
SAY ~It would seem so...I will have to think on this.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1h
SAY ~You have no idea what you are missing. It is quite enjoyable.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1o
SAY ~There is no shortage of weak-willed fools around. I am confident we will both find willing slaves, I will enjoy the hunt for one.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1p
SAY ~I too shall take great pleasure in the torture. Even if I only get to watch.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1x
SAY ~Nor did I but there are many shady things going on in this city, and slavery is a very profitable trade.~ 
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1y
SAY ~I noticed many since I arrived here and there is plenty of coin to be made with slaves. Too bad it is illegal.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1z
SAY ~Agreed. I have no fear of insulting anyone or provoking a fight but we both have more important matters at hand.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1za
SAY ~It is nice indeed, though I have always had slaves and never had to do many things myself. Not having one now has left me in a terrible position.~
++ ~Surely you did some things for yourself like getting dressed or bathing... something.~ + FT1zb
++ ~Well then, no time like the present to learn and I will be more than happy to help you in anyway I can.~  + FT1zc
++ ~Who knows.. maybe you will find some weak-willed man along the way that you can convince to be your willing slave.~  + FT1zd
++ ~Guess you will figure it soon enough. I think it is time we get going.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1zb
SAY ~Not really, no. But I had better find a solution fast, my blade needs sharpening.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1zc
SAY ~Thank you. Oh and when we make camp, my blade needs sharpening.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT1zd
SAY ~I had not thought of that! I hope I find someone soon, my blade needs sharpening .~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~Global("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",4)~ THEN BEGIN FT2
SAY ~I would like to talk to you more about what happened with the mage. I can still see shadows of pain on your face.~
++ ~I was kept in a cage and tortured, the pain was unbearable and I passed out from it. I do remember there was an explosion..~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",5) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~  + FT2a
++ ~It is not easy to talk about, being kept in a cage... the bastard murdered two of my friends!~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",5) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~  + FT2d
++ ~I do not remember much, the cage... torture and then an explosion. It was very unnerving.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",5) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT2g
++ ~I would rather not discuss it.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",5) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2a
SAY ~Why would he do such a thing? I find it odd he would kidnap a random stranger and do things like that without reason. And what of the explosion?~
++ ~He claimed to know me though I do not see how. But, after the explosion, Imoen showed up and opened my cage.~ + FT2b
++ ~He said he was doing it unlock my power, whatever that means. The explosion was odd but it distracted him long enough for Imoen to open my cage and we escaped.~  + FT2h
++ ~I do not know but I intend to find out. He has forced me to go after him by taking Imoen.~  + FT2l
++ ~I will not have the answers until I find him. Standing here will not get us any closer so let's just go.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2b
SAY ~Very odd indeed. No idea what caused the explosion and how it is that Imoen was free to help you?~
++ ~I have no idea, it is all very confusing. All I know is, he has forced me to go after him by taking Imoen and murdering two of my friends.~ + FT2c
++ ~I do not know, it is all so upsetting. I miss the friends I lost by his hand and feel responsible for their deaths.~  + FT2c
++ ~He's a madman, he probably kidnapped the wrong person by mistake. It is just sad that he killed two of my friends before Imoen helped me escape.~  + FT2c
++ ~It is still too painful to talk about, I am sorry.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2c
SAY ~I am sorry about your friends, it is hard to lose people you care about. And fear not, we will find Imoen and exact revenge on him.~
++ ~Thank you, I miss them terribly. I cannot help but feel like it is my fault they are dead.~  + FT2d
++ ~Their deaths are unimportant, they annoyed me when they were around anyway. It is Irenicus I want to get my hands on, we have much to discuss...like removing his head.~  + FT2m
++ ~I do not care if we find Imoen or not, ordering me around in that dungeon as if she had the right to do so! The mage however, I will tear him to pieces.~  + FT2n
++ ~Agreed. But not by standing here chatting. Let's get back to it.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2d
SAY ~I fail to see how it was your fault, it was not you who did the killing. Focus on the revenge you will soon claim, it will give you strength.~
++ ~I may not have struck the blow, by they died because I put them in harms way because they were with me. And revenge is not what this is about, it is justice for the crimes Irenicus committed.~  + FT2e
++ ~No, I did not kill them, though I thought about it a couple times. I see your point, I am not to blame for any of it. And yes, thinking of what I will do to that fool when I find him is all I am focusing on.~  +FT2g
++ ~You are right of course, I should not waste my time feeling sorry for the loss of those I did not even like. I just want that mage dead, and maybe a little torture first to repay him.~  +FT2o
++ ~I suppose so. Either way, we should catch up with the others.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2e
SAY ~They willingly followed you, <CHARNAME>, they knew the risks involved by doing so. And calling it revenge or justice, it is still what you should be concentrating on.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2g
SAY ~I find that all very disturbing. How did you escape, the explosion?~
++ ~The explosion was a welcomed distraction, it allowed Imoen time to open my cage.~  + FT2p
++ ~So do I. Too bad it did not kill that bastard mage at the same time. But, Imoen showed up, opened my cage and we got out of there.~  + FT2p 
++ ~That and painful... sad... Let's just get going.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2o
SAY ~That is a terrible thing to say about your companions <CHARNAME>, their deaths served no purpose.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2p
SAY ~But I am curious as to what caused the explosion in the first place, it sounds like a trap.~
++ ~Oh I am sure it is a trap, he wants me back in his grasp. He claims he was trying to unlock a hidden power within me. And the explosion was very odd.~  + FT2b
++ ~Well of course it is a trap! What I find odd is that explosion... I know that idiot did not cause it.~  + FT2b
++ ~And he better hope he's prepared because I intend to his his trap blow up in his face. Too bad that mysterious explosion did not do that already.~  + FT2b
++ ~I know it is. And I cannot wait to see what's in store, so let's get to it.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2l
SAY ~I myself am curious to know also and I agree, it seems he took her for that very reason. I sense a trap waiting for you.~
++ ~Oh I am sure it is a trap, he wants me back in his grasp. He claims he was trying to unlock a hidden power within me. And the explosion was very odd.~  + FT2b
++ ~Well of course it is a trap! What I find odd is that explosion... I know that idiot did not cause it.~  + FT2b
++ ~And he better hope he's prepared, because I intend to his his trap blow up in his face. Too bad that mysterious explosion did not do that already.~  + FT2b
++ ~I know it is. And I cannot wait to see what's in store, so let's get to it.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2h
SAY ~You have a power that you do not know about and he has to be the one to unlock it? That sounds as odd as the explosion, as you say. I am just glad you managed to get away from that fiend.~
++ ~That is what he claims but it makes no sense to me. And yes, I am very glad to be away from that nightmare, though it will take time for the scars to go away.~  + FT2i
++ ~Who knows? He sounded like a babbling madman to me, he is probably just insane. Though I am glad to have escaped, the explosion troubles me. I want to know who caused it.~  + FT2q
++ ~I plan to ask him about that before I kill him. If I do have such a power, it will be useful. Especially if it helps me kill my enemies faster.~  + FT2r
++ ~We will not find any answers here, it is time we were off.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2i
SAY ~I find it strange as well. Scars? Are you injured badly?~
++ ~More emotional scars than anything else. I have been having nightmares even since I got out of there.~  + FT2j
++ ~Not so badly that I cannot do what must be done, though I am a bit sore. The emotion scars are another matter, the nightmares are horrible.~ + FT2j
++ ~That is none of your business.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2j
SAY ~ I.. I am sorry to hear you are having nightmares, it must have been terrible for you. If there is anything I can do, do not hesitate to ask. As far as the physical scars, I have an ointment that will greatly help.~
++ ~The nightmares I will have to deal with myself, but I will gladly accept the ointment, and thank you.~  + FT2k
++ ~I do not need your sympathy or anything else from you, except your loyalty. You will do well to remember that.~ + FT2t
++ ~I will be fine, the nightmares and the pain fuel my anger, and keep me focused on the kill. And make no mistake, I will kill him, slowly.~  + FT2u
++ ~Save your pity for someone who might actually believe it is real. Let's go.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2k
SAY ~You are most welcome.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2m
SAY ~No death is unimportant, <CHARNAME>. There is no honor in a pointless death. As for Irenicus, his death is justified and he deserves that fate.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2n
SAY ~That is a terrible thing to say about the woman who saved you, <CHARNAME>, she was probably scared.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2q
SAY ~I myself am curious to know also, I sense a trap waiting for you.~
++ ~Oh I am sure it is a trap, he wants me back in his grasp. He claims he was trying to unlock a hidden power within me. And the explosion was very odd.~  + FT2b
++ ~Well of course it is a trap! What I find odd is that explosion... I know that idiot did not cause it.~  + FT2b
++ ~And he better hope he's prepared, because I intend to his his trap blow up in his face. Too bad that mysterious explosion did not do that already.~  + FT2b
++ ~I know it is. And I cannot wait to see what's in store, so let's get to it.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2r 
SAY ~Be careful what you wish for.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2s
SAY ~Scars? Are you injured badly?~
++ ~More emotional scars than anything else. I have been having nightmares even since I got out of there.~  + FT2j
++ ~Not so badly that I cannot do what must be done, though I am a bit sore. The emotion scars are another matter, the nightmares are horrible.~  + FT2j
++ ~That is none of your business.~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2t
SAY ~So be it, you will hear nothing from me.~
IF ~~ THEN DO ~SetGlobal("KKNavarFriendActive","GLOBAL",3)~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT2u
SAY ~Smart woman, you will need that in the days to come.~ 
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~Global("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",6)~ THEN BEGIN FT3
SAY ~I have heard whispers, fearful ones directed at you. They say you are a bhaalspawn, what does that mean?~
++ ~It means my father is Bhaal, the God of Murder.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",7) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT3b
++ ~I have no idea why anyone would say that. I would not believe everything you hear.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",7) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT3v
++ ~A bhaalspawn is a child of Bhaal, the God of Murder. It is his blood that flows through my veins.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",7) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT3b
++ ~I would rather not discuss it.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",7) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~  EXIT 
END

IF ~~ FT3b
SAY ~Bhaal? How can that be...~
++ ~I was even more surprised to find that out than you are, trust me.~ + FT3c
++ ~I assume your not familiar with the prophecy of Alaundo?~ + FT3t
++ ~Does that bother you?~ + FT3u
++ ~Let's just go, shall we?~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3c
SAY ~It must have been difficult to deal with as a child.~
++ ~I was not told until recently.~ + FT3d
++ ~My foster father kept that from me as a child. The old fool ended up telling me in a letter that I found after he died.~ + FT3e
++ ~My foster father, Gorion, never told me. I guess he wanted me to have a normal childhood.~ + FT3r
++ ~I would rather not discuss it.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3d
SAY ~I do not understand. If your birth mother kept that from you all this time, why tell you now?~
++ ~I was not raised by my mother, I was raised by my foster father, Gorion. And he did not tell me, I found a letter he had written to me before he died.~ + FT3e
++ ~I do not know who my mother is. my foster father, Gorion, raised me. I assume he did not tell me because he wanted me to have a normal childhood.~ + FT3r
++ ~Why would you assume I was raised by my mother?~ + FT3s
++ ~I assume your not familiar with the prophecy of Alaundo?~ + FT3t
++ ~It does not matter, let's go.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3e
SAY ~What happened to your birth mother? And please explain "foster father", it is a term I am unfamiliar with.~
++ ~I have no idea, I never knew her. A foster father is a man who assumes the role of a father when your real one is gone.~ + FT3f
++ ~She obviously abandoned me, I have no memory of her. And a foster father is not much different from a father, just a replacement.~ + FT3q
++ ~A foster father is not much different from a father, I assume you know what father means.~ + FT3f
++ ~I do not know what happened to her and I do not care. Gorion was the only parent I needed. He is my real father, as far as I am concerned.~ + FT3q
++ ~I do not want to talk about this anymore. Let's go.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3f
SAY ~I am sorry, but I do not know what "father" means either. I can only assume you mean the man who assisted your mother when she decided to become pregnant.~
= ~You talk as if a father has another purpose besides the obvious one.~
++ ~Usually he does, but I assume in your case, he does not. Is your father a slave?~ + FT3g
++ ~Normally children are raised by both parents. But because my mother left and my father was Bhaal, Gorion took me in, and took care of me.~ + FT3g
++ ~They do but I hated it, I am glad the old fool is dead and I am finally free to do as I wish.~ + FT3n
++ ~Enough of this, we should get going.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3g
SAY ~There are no men in my tribe except slaves. Our tribe would die out without children, so they serve in that task as well.~
++ ~Do you at least know which slave is your father?~ + FT3h
++ ~I am sorry, I cannot imagine what it must be like to grow up without a father.~ + FT3k
++ ~Your lucky you did not have to put up with one like I did.~ + FT3m
++ ~I do not want to talk about this anymore. Let's go.~ EXIT
END 

IF ~~ FT3h
SAY ~The female children are never told but, it usually is not hard to figure out. If you care to, that is. Inherited features, even certain traits give it away.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3l
END

IF ~~ FT3i
SAY ~It must be hard for you to keep it under control as you do. You have my respect.~
IF ~~  EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3j
SAY ~Power can be a dangerous thing when used for evil, <CHARNAME>. I hope you come to realize the folly of that goal before it is too late.~
IF ~~  EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3k
SAY ~That is because you had one and know the difference. For my people, it is a normal way of life. You cannot miss what you never had, and never knew existed.~
= ~We are all aware that a slave aided in our birth, but never which one. It usually is not hard to figure out. If you care to, that is. Inherited features, even certain traits give it away.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3l
END

IF ~~ FT3l
SAY ~Is it like that for you, with Bhaal being your father?~
++ ~The blood lust is always there, and a constant struggle. But I have managed to keep it under control, so far.~ + FT3i
++ ~Certainly, there is no doubt his blood flows through my veins. I can feel the power, the lust for blood in battle.~ + FT3i
++ ~Of course and I am glad of it. I have a destiny to fulfill, to sit on his throne one day and I need all the power I can get.~ + FT3j
++ ~I will let you find that out for yourself.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3m
SAY ~Perhaps...It is impossible to say since I never had one. We are all aware that a slave aided in our birth, but never which one. It usually is not hard to figure out. If you care to, that is. Inherited features, even certain traits give it away.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3l
END

IF ~~ FT3n
SAY ~And what is it that you wish to do?~
++ ~Fulfill my destiny of course. Sit on my father's throne and rule in his place.~ + FT3j
++ ~All I want is a normal life, though it seems impossible with this prophecy hanging over my head and everyone trying to kill me.~ + FT3o
++ ~I want to keep traveling, helping people and seeing new places.~ + FT3p
++ ~I do not know yet, but I like being able to make my own decisions and seeing where they take me.~ + FT3p
++ ~Catch up with the others, they are starting to get impatient.~ EXIT
END  

IF ~~ FT3o
SAY ~I do not know of this prophecy but I have no doubt it is of evil intent, but never give up hope. Anything is possible when we rule our destinies, instead of letting them rule us.~
= ~You have my respect.~
IF ~~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3p
SAY ~Just avoid Narfell, unless you do not mind freezing to death in the winter.~
IF ~~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT3q
SAY ~That sounds much like what happens in my tribe. Male children are raised as slaves so, they have no memory of who their birth mother is either.~
= ~But this other role...~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3f
END

IF ~~ FT3r
SAY ~I do not know what a normal childhood is by your definition, but this man must have cared for you greatly.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3e
END

IF ~~ FT3s
SAY ~I assumed that is how it is done where you are from. In my tribe, male children are raised by slaves because they will become slaves themselves.~
= ~And a dead God cannot raise you....I...~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3f
END

IF ~~ FT3t
SAY ~I do not. But any prophecy connected to Bhaal can only end in death and destruction. You are fortunate that you were not raised by such an evil being.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3f
END

IF ~~ FT3u
SAY ~I...I do not know yet. It would depend on how much of his influence lies within you, and so far I have seen nothing to convince me that you have an evil nature.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT3c
END

IF ~~ FT3v
SAY ~There must be some truth to it, if so many believe it to be so.~
++ ~Fine. If you must know, it means my father is Bhaal, the God of Murder.~ + FT3b
++ ~Well there is not, so just let it go.~ EXIT
END

IF ~Global("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",8)~ THEN BEGIN FT4
SAY ~You mentioned that Gorian was murdered, do you know by who?~
++ ~Gorion was murdered a year ago, when he and I left our home in Candlekeep.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",9) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT4a
++ ~He's dead, leave it at that.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",9) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT4g
++ ~It is a painful subject, I would rather not talk about it.~DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",9) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~  + FT4h
++ ~It does not concern you, let's get going.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",9) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~  EXIT
END 

IF ~~ FT4a
SAY ~I... I am sorry to hear that <CHARNAME>. Do you know who did such a terrible thing?~
++ ~Thank you, I miss him a lot. And yes, the monster's name was Sarevok.~ + FT4b
++ ~Yes I do and he was dealt with.~ + FT4i
++ ~Thank you, it is been very hard on me without him. He was murdered by a fiend named Sarevok.~ + FT4b
++ ~It is not any of your business.~ EXIT 
END

IF ~~ FT4b
SAY ~I assume since you know the vile creature's name, that he was punished.~
++ ~I killed him. And I know his name because he is my brother, well half-brother. A fact I am not proud of.~ + FT4c
++ ~He left me no choice but to kill him, and his name is Sarevok.~ + FT4c
++ ~Yes he was punished, I killed that bastard, and I enjoyed it. Unfortunately, he is my brother.~ + FT4j
++ ~I would really rather not talk about it. We should really catch up to the others.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4c
SAY ~Murderers deserve nothing less than death, I am glad he no longer lives.~
++ ~My thoughts exactly, he was too dangerous to be allowed to live. I just wish Gorion had not faced him alone, but he insisted.~ + FT4d
++ ~I did not kill him because he killed Gorion, I killed him because he was a Child of Bhaal also.~ + FT4g
++ ~Yes, and the rest does not matter anymore. Let's go.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4d
SAY ~It was brave of him to face so many alone so that you could get away safely. He must have loved you a great deal.~
++ ~Gorion was a mage of great skill, I honestly expected him to defeat Sarevok easily.~ + FT4e
++ ~Yes, it was but, I have no doubt that he expected to put and end to Sarevok that day. Sadly, it did not work out that way.~ + FT4e
++ ~Gorion was like that. He always let me know he loved me, and protected me too much sometimes. I still cannot believe he's dead.~ + FT4f
++ ~It was foolish of him to even try. That over-bearing moron got what he deserved.~ + FT4k
++ ~It is too painful to talk about right now. Perhaps we should get going.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4e 
SAY ~It is not easy to kill a powerful mage, do you know what went wrong?~
++ ~It seems Sarevok had a high resistance to magic. Gorion's spells did not even affect him so he did not stand a chance at defeating him.~ + FT4f
++ ~Sarevok had no reason to fear Gorion and he knew it, his resistance to magic made him a formidable foe.~ + FT4f
+ ~Class(Player1,MAGE_ALL)~ + ~I found out the hard way that magic does not affect him. But in the end, it did not matter if he died by magic or blade. Only that he died.~ + FT4l
++ ~How could I when I told you I was not there. Let's go.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4f
SAY ~I am sorry you lost Gorian, <CHARNAME>, but I am glad you were able to kill his murderer. I am sure Gorion would be very proud of you.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4g
SAY ~You sound as if you are glad Gorion died, surely that is not so.~
++ ~I am sorry, it just is not easy to talk about. He was murdered a year ago and it is still quite painful.~ + FT4a
++ ~I am, he lied to me about who I am... I am glad to rid of the old fool.~ + FT4k
++ ~Believe what you will. We have to get to Irenicus, that is what matters now.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4h
SAY ~I understand but sometimes it helps to have an ear. I am here if you change your mind.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4i
SAY ~So you killed him, I hope. Was it someone you knew?~
++ ~I killed him, yes. And I know his name because he is my brother, well half-brother. A fact I am not proud of.~ + FT4c
++ ~He left me no choice but to kill him and his name is Sarevok.~ + FT4c
++ ~I killed that bastard and I enjoyed it. Unfortunately, he is my brother.~ + FT4c
++ ~I would really rather not talk about it. We should really catch up to the others.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4j
SAY ~I too would have enjoyed giving a murderer what they deserve. I do hope you did not witness the murder.~
++ ~Thankfully, I did not see it. Gorion told me to run when Sarevok and two of his henchmen showed up.~ + FT4d
++ ~Sadly no, Gorion ordered me to run when Sarevok and two of his henchmen showed up.~ + FT4d
++ ~I wish I had been there, Gorion would still be alive. Taking on all three villians was madness. But no, I was told to run.~ + FT4m
++ ~None of it matters now, let's be off.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4k
SAY ~That is horrible, <CHARNAME>. There is no honor in murder and no one deserves to die that way.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4l
SAY ~He deserved no less, and I am glad you survived the ordeal.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ FT4m
SAY ~I understand your wanting to be there but, I must confess, I am glad you were not.~
IF ~~ THEN + FT4d
END

IF ~Global("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",10)~ THEN BEGIN FT5
SAY ~I would very much like to hear about your home.~ 
++ ~I no longer have a home.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",11) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT5a
++ ~I grew up in Candlekeep. I was raised by monks.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",11) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT5d
++ ~Imoen and I grew up in Candlekeep. We had a normal childhood, I suppose for children being raised by monks.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",11) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ + FT5n
++ ~I do not want to talk about it.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNFTalk","GLOBAL",11) RealSetGlobalTimer("KKFemaleTalkTime","GLOBAL",1800)~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5a
SAY ~Why not? You do not want to return, after all this is over?~
++ ~I went back to Candlekeep, not too long ago. The monks informed me that I am no longer welcome there because of what I am.~ + FT5b
++ ~The monks fear me now, being a Child of Bhaal.~ + FT5i
++ ~The monks never wanted me there. They only let me because of Gorion.~ + FT5j
++ ~No, I hated that place. Let's go.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5b
SAY ~Because of you being a Child of Bhaal?~ 
IF ~~ THEN + FT5i 
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5i
SAY ~That is unjust of them. They raised you, and know you to be a good man.~
++ ~They have the right to feel as they do. I never intended to live there forever, anyway.~ + FT5d
++ ~They are wise to fear me, and I will make them pay for how they treated me.~ + FT5e
++ ~I really do not care what they think. We need to catch up with the others.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5d
SAY ~Was your childhood unpleasant there?~
++ ~No, the monks were nice enough to me. Imoen made it enjoyable, she was always playing jokes on them.~ + FT5f
++ ~Extremely, and Imoen made it worse. The little prankster was always getting us in trouble.~ + FT5g
++ ~I liked it well enough. I loved to read and the library is quite large.~ + FT5h
++ ~It does not matter anymore.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5e
SAY ~I hope you do not mean that.~ 
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5f
SAY ~I am sure she had a good reason, I cannot imagine being raised in such a place.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5g
SAY ~I imagine it was difficult for both of you. Being raised by a male would be bad enough...~
= ~But, monks would be much worse, I think.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5h
SAY ~I enjoy reading myself. I always managed to find a book or two at our yearly festival.~
= ~But nothing like the amount you are used to.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5j
SAY ~They must have known all along about your heritage, and chose not to tell you.~
++ ~They did. As soon as Gorion died, they had no reason to allow me back there.~ + FT5k
++ ~Exactly, and when that fool Gorion was killed, they turned their backs on me.~ + FT5m
++ ~They will regret that decision once I take the throne.~ + FT5e
++ ~Most likely, but it does not matter now.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5k
SAY ~They should have had faith in you, that you would do what was right.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5m
SAY ~I cannot say that I blame them. Not when you intend to use the throne for evil.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5n
SAY ~I cannot imagine growing up in the confines of a keep. Though I am sure it made the winters bearable.~
++ ~It was not so bad. The monks were strict at times, but they had reason to be. The winters aren't bad at all.~ + FT5o
++ ~It was fascinating to me. The towers, fortress.. a lot to explore. The winters were rough for you?~ + FT5p
++ ~I cannot imagine growing up outside without the protection of walls.~ + FT5q
++ ~I have no desire to discuss Candlekeep.~ EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5o
SAY ~Strict or not, you were fortunate. Surviving the frigid winters in Narfell is difficult.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5p
SAY ~I can see why you enjoyed it.~
= ~The frigid winters in Narfell are difficult to survive. It is especially dangerous for our elders and small babies.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~~ THEN FT5q
SAY ~I see your point. We both grew up in very different ways.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT
END

IF ~Global("KKNavarRSoulTalk","LOCALS",1)~  THEN BEGIN KKNSoul1
SAY ~<CHARNAME>... What has happened to you?~
++ ~I cannot say for certain. I would have never thought it possible, but somehow Irenicus has taken my soul, and Imoen's as well. It seems she is a child of Bhaal also.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNavarRSoulTalk","LOCALS",2)~ + KKNSoul1a
++ ~Irenicus cast a spell. I am fine, do not worry. We need to get out of here, quickly.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNavarRSoulTalk","LOCALS",2)~ + KKNSoul1b
++ ~Now is not the time to talk, I have to get Imoen out of here.~ DO ~SetGlobal("KKNavarRSoulTalk","LOCALS",2)~ + KKNSoul1c
END

IF ~~ THEN KKNSoul1a
SAY ~How dare he! Lean on me, if you need to, but we have to get out of here.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN KKNSoul1b
SAY ~No, you are not. You will be, of that I can promise you.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT 
END

IF ~~ THEN KKNSoul1c
SAY ~Indeed, forgive me. We will talk about this once we are all safely away from this place.~
IF ~~ THEN EXIT 
END

IF ~Global("KKNavarCSoulTalk","LOCALS",1)~ THEN BEGIN KKNSoul2
SAY ~What has happened to you, my love. You do not look well.~
